            <ArticleTitle>Women's health. Factors linking women and CHD.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>29-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Is coronary heart disease in women receiving the attention it deserves? Much of the advice on the prevention of CHD has been focused on men, and women tend to concentrate on reducing their families' risk of heart disease rather than their own. This paper investigates the importance of the disease in women and examines the way certain aspects of women's lives can have an adverse effect on their health.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
